ute for the financial information prepared and presented in accordance with U.S. GAAP. We present these non-GAAP financial measures because they are used by our management to evaluate our operating performance and formulate business plans. We also believe that the use of these non-GAAP measures facilitates investors’ assessment of our operating performance.","context":"Non-GAAP Financial Measures","section":"Results of Operations","block":66,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-395514","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-18","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001979887","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979887/000119312526395514/ck0001979887-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0d00c2ea621ce97c08278fa86f8d18bc27ef658656eeb57350addf3130d5e64c.bin","sha256":"0d00c2ea621ce97c08278fa86f8d18bc27ef658656eeb57350addf3130d5e64c"}},{"id":"924e4632bf6c011a01827e139d0c74dd93c0378dd79fa019bd730a7ba44c4775","quote":"These non-GAAP financial measures are not defined under U.S. GAAP and are not presented in accordance with U.S. GAAP. These non-GAAP financial measures have limitations as analytical tools. One of the key limitations of using these non-GAAP financial measures is that they do not reflect all items of income and expense that affect our operations. Further, these non-GAAP measures may differ from the non-GAAP information used by other companies, including peer companies, and therefore their comparability may be limited. We compensate for these limitations by reconciling these non-GAAP financial measures to the nearest U.S. GAAP performance measures, all of which should be considered when evaluating our performance. We encourage you to review our financial information in its entirety and not rely on a single financial measure.","context":"We consider non-GAAP net loss and non-GAAP basic and diluted loss per Class A and Class B ordinary share as supplemental measures to review and assess our operating performance. The presentation of these non-GAAP financial measures is not intended to be considered in isolation or as a substitute for the financial information prepared and presented in accordance with U.S. GAAP. We present these non-GAAP financial measures because they are used by our management to evaluate our operating performance and formulate business plans. We also believe that the use of these non-GAAP measures facilitates investors’ assessment of our operating performance.","section":"Results of Operations","block":67,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-395514","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-18","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001979887","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979887/000119312526395514/ck0001979887-ex99_1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/0d00c2ea621ce97c08278fa86f8d18bc27ef658656eeb57350addf3130d5e64c.bin","sha256":"0d00c2ea621ce97c08278fa86f8d18bc27ef658656eeb57350addf3130d5e64c"}},{"id":"9ceaad655591561e0852589bbfb96a82966c834fa8b279131451c2668890a0d7","quote":"We define non-GAAP net loss as net loss excluding share-based compensation and changes in fair value of financial instruments. We define non-GAAP basic and diluted loss per Class A and Class B ordinary share as non-GAAP net loss divided by the weighted average number of Class A and Class B ordinary shares outstanding during the period.","context":"These non-GAAP financial measures are not defined under U.S. GAAP and are not presented in accordance with U.S. GAAP. These non-GAAP financial measures have limitations as analytical tools. One of the key limitations of using these non-GAAP financial measures is that they do not reflect all items of income and expense that affect our operations. Further, these non-GAAP measures may differ from the non-GAAP information used by other companies, including peer companies, and therefore their comparability m